On ModelHub, we use AI in two ways: how we build, and what we build.
The first is AIDLC, our AI-driven development lifecycle. It helps the team analyse, build, review and document work efficiently.
The second is a set of AI agents built into the product. The data for payment standards like ISO 8583, ISO 20022 and Nexo is spread across PDFs, Excel sheets, Word documents, XSD schemas and GitHub repositories, each with its own format and structure. Before ModelHub, users had to go through all of these sources, work out which parts were relevant, match them up and enter everything by hand. That took [X] hours per release and made it easy to miss or misread something. Our agents now go through every one of these sources and pull out the relevant fields, rules and mappings. They match them up across sources, turn them into structured data and seed it into the ModelHub database for the team to review.
Next, we plan to bring AI into business workflows such as maker-checker and version comparison.
